     "text": "Done. The render confirms the layout: centerline into the bulb, both edges stopping at the circle.\n\n## 1. What was created and drawn\n- **Alignment OAK-CT**: BEGIN [3000.00, 2000.00] (N 2000, E 3000) at 10+00.00, one tangent N 00°00'00\" E, 400.00 ft, END [3000.00, 2400.00] at 14+00.00.\n- **LN-001** – centerline on `align_MAIN`, [3000, 2000] → [3000, 2400] (anchored to OAK-CT).\n- **CI-001** – cul-de-sac bulb on `rd_EP`, circle center [3000, 2400], R = 45.00.\n- **LN-002** – left EP (14L) on `rd_EP`, [2986, 2000] → [2986, 2357.23], 357.23 ft.\n- **LN-003** – right EP (14R) on `rd_EP`, [3014, 2000] → [3014, 2357.23], 357.23 ft.\n  Both edges stop exactly on the bulb circle and keep their design-offset anchors.\n\n## 2. Tool calls that mattered\n1. `get_document_state` – confirmed empty model; layers `align_MAIN` and `rd_EP` already existed.\n2. `create_alignment` name=OAK-CT, begin_station=\"10+00\", start=[3000, 2000], legs=[{bearing \"N 0°00'00\\\" E\", distance 400}].\n3. `draw_alignment` alignment=OAK-CT, layer=align_MAIN → LN-001.\n4. `draw_circle` center=[3000, 2400], radius=45, layer=rd_EP → CI-001.\n5. `draw_offset` alignment=OAK-CT, offsets=[-14, 14], layer=rd_EP → LN-002, LN-003 (full length, through the bulb).\n6. `trim` targets=[{LN-002, at [2986, 2390]}, {LN-003, at [3014, 2390]}], boundaries=[CI-001] → 42.77 ft cut from each.\n7. `get_entity` ×2 and `render_model` to verify.\n\n## 3. Problems / workarounds / arithmetic\n- Nothing failed; no error messages.\n- Only hand arithmetic was choosing the trim pick points (the engine computed the actual intersections): the circle meets an edge at offset 14 where y = 2400 − √(45² − 14²) = 2400 − √(2025 − 196) = 2400 − √1829 ≈ 2400 − 42.77 = 2357.23, so a pick at y = 2390 lies on the piece inside the bulb. The trim result (42.77 ft removed, 357.23 ft kept, end y = 2357.2332) matches."
